Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 02:53:30 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 03/23] Sheet-TPMS true-geometry label route: no port collars,
 carrier 1/32, exact rigid reproduction

The cell geometry used so far carried 1/32 solid plates on all six box faces (46% of the G0 material) and treated the
world cut as a port. Both are removed: the material is now the sheet |phi| <= tau clipped by the box and the cut, and
the cut surface is free. Volume validated against the published Schwarz-P density law C = 1.755 rho (Hao 2023,
Dalian UT): our exact integration gives rho = 0.2284 where the law predicts 0.2279 (+0.23%); the mesh reproduces it to
0.16%. The collar geometry gave 0.387.

- sheet_solid_surface.py: marching cubes + exact Newton projection onto the level set, exact plane clipping, boundary
  collapse and pymeshlab remeshing with re-projection, box-corner restoration, carrier-conforming band caps by
  constrained Delaunay (Triangle in a subprocess, planar arrangement of the constraints), confidence-weighted region
  flood fill, T-junction repair, floating-fragment removal, Gmsh volume mesh.
- Active carrier set is a superset of any mesher support, so the port map keeps exact partition of unity, affine and
  rigid reproduction (residual 1e-14; a clip-and-renormalize variant that cost 1e-6 was removed).
- Carrier grid per face is a parameter; 1/32 is the decision of record.
- Owner decisions: empty cells skipped, fragments not connected to a port face removed, narrow bands labeled as they are.
- Measured: mesher reproducibility 0.12-0.56%, three-level mesh convergence 1.4% at 0.03 and 0.7% at 0.02, 2x1x1 block
  assembly interface error 0.1% (smooth loads) with the whole remaining deficit on the loaded external face.

